An empty path argument (as an unset shell variable in `outln "$dir"` makes) is a usage error with exit 2, rather than a glob view of the working directory.
== args
input/a.md

== file input/a.md
# a
== stdout
== stderr
error: invalid value '' for '<PATH>...': a path can't be empty; use . for the working directory

For more information, try '--help'.
== exit 2
